A sandbox reaches the network only through its supervisor's policy DNS and
proxy. Policy DNS answers every AAAA query with NODATA and resolves only A
records upstream, so in an IPv6-only cluster no sandbox can resolve a name
(policy_dns_upstream_no_data). #3702 adds a policy_dns_ipv6_egress mode (auto
answers AAAA when the supervisor's namespace has an IPv6 default route and no
IPv4 one), NAT64-aware SSRF checks, and driver settings to pass both to the
supervisor.

Rebase notes: architecture/sandbox.md was deleted upstream and is dropped; the
docker and podman drivers keep both v0.1.3's proxy CA bundle and the PR's
ipv6_egress settings; v0.1.3 moved run_sandbox's arguments into
SandboxRunConfig, so the PR's two new ones are carried there too; the
Kubernetes driver's supervisor_pod tests pass both v0.1.3's
tracing_environment and the PR's ipv6_egress_args.

